TC-S2-TST-02: Customer Create & Edit Form Validation Rules
Test Component: Customer Create & Edit Form
Test Description: Verify that customer creation and edit forms persist valid payloads while enforcing required field constraints, 
column length limits (custno VARCHAR(5), custname VARCHAR(20)), and payterm check constraints (pay_ck: 'COD', '30D', '45D').

Test Steps:
-Open the Create Customer form, submit valid customer values (custno, custname, address, payterm), and confirm persistence in public.customer.
-Edit an existing customer's details and verify the updated record saves cleanly.
-Attempt to submit blank required fields, oversized strings, or disallowed payterm values (e.g., '60D' or NULL).

Expected Result: Valid creates and updates succeed cleanly, while invalid inputs trigger clear validation 
errors and are blocked at both UI and database (pay_ck / NOT NULL) boundaries.
Actual Result: Form validation rules and database pay_ck / NOT NULL constraints verified across positive and negative payloads.


Status: PASS ✅

TC-S2-TST-03: Customer Soft Delete & Account Restoration Workflow
Test Component: Customer Soft Delete & Restore (S2-DEV-03 / S2-TST-01)
Test Description: Verify that soft-deleting a customer populates deleted_at and hides the record from active customer views, 
while restoring sets deleted_at = NULL and returns the customer to active status.

Test Steps:
-Trigger soft delete on an active customer and verify it disappears from the active Customer List
-Inspect public.customer / archived filter view to confirm the record remains intact with a non-null deleted_at timestamp.
-Trigger the restore action on the soft-deleted customer and confirm deleted_at resets to NULL and the record reappears in the active directory.

Expected Result: Soft-deleted customers are excluded from active queries without data loss and recover cleanly upon restoration
Actual Result: Soft delete (deleted_at timestamping) and restore (deleted_at IS NULL) workflows validated cleanly.

Status: PASS ✅

TC-S2-TST-04: Role-Based Access Rights & Permission Enforcement
Test Component: Customer Module Permission Checks
Test Description: Verify that role-based access rights strictly restrict viewing, creating, editing, soft-deleting, 
and restoring customers to authorized users across both frontend routes and backend API endpoints.

Test Steps:
-Log in as a standard user lacking Customer Management rights and confirm Customer UI actions/routes are hidden or blocked.
-Attempt direct API calls (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE, PATCH) to customer endpoints using an unauthorized session token.
-Log in as an authorized user/admin with explicit Customer permissions and verify full authorized access.

Expected Result: Unauthorized accounts receive 403 Forbidden (or 401 Unauthorized when unauthenticated) on restricted endpoints, while authorized accounts operate normally.
Actual Result: Role-based access controls verified at both UI navigation and backend API middleware layers.

Status: PASS ✅
